# Game Assets & Memory-Leak Rules

## 1 · Audio — defer until first interaction

Never create an `Audio` element at component mount time.
Create it only inside the first `keydown` / `pointerdown` handler, and set `preload = 'none'`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fetches audio on cold page load
useEffect(() => {
  const el = new Audio('/audio/track.mp3');
  el.play().catch(() => {});
}, []);

// ✅ GOOD — deferred, no network request until the user acts
useEffect(() => {
  let el: HTMLAudioElement | null = null;
  const start = () => {
    if (el) { el.play().catch(() => {}); return; }
    el = new Audio('/audio/track.mp3');
    el.preload = 'none';
    el.loop    = true;
    el.play().catch(() => {});
  };
  window.addEventListener('keydown',     start, { once: true });
  window.addEventListener('pointerdown', start, { once: true });
  return () => {
    el?.pause();
    window.removeEventListener('keydown',     start);
    window.removeEventListener('pointerdown', start);
  };
}, []);
```

## 2 · Future sprite assets

Any new sprite, icon, or texture file must be **WebP** format.
PNG/JPEG are not acceptable for new assets added to `/public`.

## 3 · useEffect cleanup — mandatory checklist

Every `useEffect` that registers an async resource **must** return a cleanup function.

| Resource | Cleanup |
|---|---|
| `requestAnimationFrame` | `cancelAnimationFrame(id)` |
| `setInterval` | `clearInterval(id)` |
| `setTimeout` (> ~100 ms) | track in a ref → `clearTimeout(ref.current)` |
| `window.addEventListener` | `window.removeEventListener(…)` |
| `AbortController` | `return () => controller.abort()` |

For short jump/animation timeouts (e.g. 560 ms), always store the id in a ref so it can be cancelled if the component unmounts mid-animation:

```tsx
const jumpTimerRef = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);

const triggerJump = () => {
  if (jumpTimerRef.current) clearTimeout(jumpTimerRef.current);
  jumpTimerRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
    jumpTimerRef.current = null;
    setJumping(false);
  }, 560);
};

// In effect cleanup:
return () => {
  if (jumpTimerRef.current) clearTimeout(jumpTimerRef.current);
};
```

## 4 · AbortController — abort on every exit path

Create a new `AbortController` at the start of each fetch effect and pass `controller.signal`.
The `return` cleanup **must** call `controller.abort()`.
Also abort immediately at the top of the effect whenever the previous fetch should be cancelled (e.g. new NPC greeting):

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!shouldFetch) return;
  prevAbortRef.current?.abort();
  const controller = new AbortController();
  prevAbortRef.current = controller;
  fetchSomething(controller.signal).catch(err => {
    if (err.name === 'AbortError') return;
    // handle real errors
  });
  return () => controller.abort(); // covers unmount AND dep-change
}, [dep]);
```

## 5 · Tiny decorative elements

Do not add SVG elements that are invisible at game scale (e.g. < 3 px on the 1400 px viewport).
Common offenders: individual window `<rect>` grids, sub-1px stroke lines with opacity < 0.2.
Replace window grids with a **single tint overlay rect** per building face.
